# Tales of Graces f Remastered (PPSA19991) — boot to gameplay (the Lhant Hill prologue).
#
# VALIDATED on Linux with hardware Vulkan (RADV, AMD Radeon 8060S / STRIX_HALO), native
# 1920x1080, headless `tools/screenshot` frontend, PROSPER_RENDER=1, no render acceleration.
#
# WHY reach-options.pad stops at the settings screen, and why Cross alone can never leave it:
# two screens in the new-game flow bind their "go" action to the **OPTIONS button**, and each
# one then raises a Yes/No dialog whose default selection is **No**.
#
#   new-game settings screen   footer: "[options] Confirm Settings   [left stick] Change"
#                              -> dialog "Confirm settings?"  Yes / [No]
#   Grade Shop                 footer: "(cross) Select   [options] Start Game   L2 R2 Scroll"
#                              -> dialog "Start the game?"   Yes / [No]
#
# So each gate is OPTIONS -> move up to Yes -> Cross. Cross alone answers No and returns to the
# same screen, which is exactly the loop reach-options.pad sits in.
#
# The directional taps are 0.15 s ON PURPOSE. A whole-second hold auto-repeats inside a
# two-entry list and lands back on No: three separate 1 s `up` windows left "Confirm settings?"
# reading No, and the same window shortened to 0.15 s moved it to Yes on the first try.
#
# Cross is safe to repeat everywhere before the first gate, which is what lets the opening
# ladder self-synchronise instead of depending on how fast the host booted: it dismisses the
# autosave dialog, skips the logos and the opening movie, advances the title screen, agrees to
# the privacy policy, selects New Game (already the default entry), and dismisses the settings
# tutorial popup — and it is unbound on the settings screen itself, so surplus presses simply
# wait there.
#
# Phases 5-6 repeat the two gates ~170 s later. Boot depth on this host varies by more than
# 200 s with machine load (the settings screen has been observed at t=90 s and at t=441 s on
# the same binary and route), so the second pass is what covers a slow boot. On a fast boot the
# game is already running when it fires; OPTIONS during the prologue raises a "[triangle] Skip"
# overlay, which the following `up` and Cross do NOT accept (the skip is bound to Triangle), so
# the overlay closes on its own and the scene carries on. Measured on both verification runs.

# --- phase 1: opening ladder — autosave dialog, logos, movie, title, privacy policy, New Game
4-5:cross
6-7:cross
8-9:cross
10-11:cross
12-13:cross
20-21:cross
30-31:cross
40-41:cross
50-51:cross
60-61:cross
70-71:cross
80-81:cross
